symfony/mcp-bundle: let a client answer roots/list

The bundle had a `clients.<name>.capabilities.roots` boolean but no way to
register a handler, so a client that set it advertised the roots capability and
then answered "method not found" to the server's `roots/list` request — which
reaches the model as an opaque protocol error.

Adds `clients.<name>.roots`, pointing at a service implementing the SDK's
`Mcp\Client\Handler\Request\RootsCallbackInterface`, and derives the advertised
capability from it exactly as `sampling` and `elicitation` already do.

[BC BREAK] `capabilities.roots` is removed. Advertising the capability without a
handler behind it was never useful; `roots: 'App\...'` replaces it.

